{"id":"p1-b11-045","paper":1,"topic":"New & renewable energy sources","kind":"fact","front":"Name the three types of geothermal power plant and how each works.","back":"Dry steam: steam from a production well drives the turbine directly, then is condensed and reinjected. Flash steam: hot water (about 182°C) is flashed to steam in a low-pressure tank. Binary cycle: lower-temperature water (107–182°C) heats a low-boiling organic working fluid (e.g. isobutane) in a heat exchanger, in two closed loops.","explain":"In all three, spent fluid is returned to the reservoir through an injection well. Because the binary cycle keeps geothermal water and working fluid in separate closed loops, it has no air emissions.","flash":false,"source":"BEE Book 1 Ch 11 p325","order":1559}
]$cards$::jsonb);
